==============================================================================
(b)  UNBEATABILITY UNDER DISCOUNTING
==============================================================================
Claim R1.  For T < S (wedge S / wedge E side, u - v > 1) the focal p is a
           discounted rival for EVERY q and every q-opening iff
               p0 = 1,  p1 = 1,  and  delta (1 - p2 - p3) <= 1 - delta.
           delta = 1 recovers the project's p2 + p3 >= 1 (and the excluded
           edge p2=1,p3=0 stops being excluded once delta < 1).

   delta                       p   p0   pred      min(v_CD - v_DC)  ok
    0.25    ['1', '0', '0', '0']    1   True                     0  OK
    0.25  ['1', '0', '1/3', '1']    1   True                     0  OK
    0.50    ['1', '0', '0', '0']    1   True                     0  OK
    0.50  ['1', '0', '1/3', '1']    1   True                     0  OK
    0.75    ['1', '0', '0', '0']    1  False                  -1/2  OK
    0.75  ['1', '0', '1/3', '1']    1  False                 -4/23  OK
    0.90    ['1', '0', '0', '0']    1  False                  -4/5  OK
    0.90  ['1', '0', '1/3', '1']    1  False               -50/157  OK
    0.95    ['1', '0', '0', '0']    1  False                 -9/10  OK
    0.95  ['1', '0', '1/3', '1']    1  False             -700/1941  OK

  80 (delta, p) pairs with p1 = 1 and p0 = 1: 0 disagreements
  between the predicate  delta(1-p2-p3) <= 1-delta  and the brute-force minimum
  of v_CD - v_DC over all 16 deterministic q and both q-openings.

Claim R2.  p0 = 1 and p1 = 1 are NECESSARY: against q = ALLC the focal is in
           CD never and in DC with positive discounted weight as soon as
           p0 < 1 or p1 < 1.
    p0=1/2 p=['1', '1', '1', '1'] vs ALLC(C): v_CD=0  v_DC=1/20  margin=-1/20
    p0=1 p=['9/10', '1', '1', '1'] vs ALLC(C): v_CD=0  v_DC=9/109  margin=-9/109

Claim R3.  T > S (every Prisoner's Dilemma): efficiency forces the focal to open
           C, rivalry forces it to open D.  Shown here for the rivalry half:
           against q = ALLD the focal is never in DC, so it must never be in CD.
    p0=1 p=ALLC vs ALLD(D): v_CD=1 v_DC=0 -> v_DC - v_CD = -1
    p0=1/2 p=ALLC vs ALLD(D): v_CD=19/20 v_DC=0 -> v_DC - v_CD = -19/20
    p0=0 p=ALLC vs ALLD(D): v_CD=9/10 v_DC=0 -> v_DC - v_CD = -9/10

Claim R4.  No memory-one strategy can ENFORCE pi_x - pi_y = const when delta < 1.
           delta p = c + (S_x - S_y) + gamma 1 needs delta p1 = 1 + gamma <= delta
           (so gamma <= delta - 1 < 0) and delta p4 = gamma >= 0.  Contradiction.
           At delta = 1 both hold with gamma = 0: the generalised-TFT line
           p = (1, 1-(T-S), T-S, 0).  Numerical illustration -- the undiscounted
           equaliser stops equalising the moment delta < 1:
    (u,v)=(6/5,0) -> T-S=-1/5; equaliser p=['1', '6/5', '-1/5', '0'] is outside the cube (p3<0), as T<S forces.  Use T>S instead:
    delta=0.99  v_DC - v_CD over 6 q's: ['-99/5050', '-19701/1495000', '-9999/529850', '-198/20099', '-99/5050', '-198/19901']
    delta=0.90  v_DC - v_CD over 6 q's: ['-9/55', '-171/1450', '-99/785', '-18/209', '-9/55', '-18/191']
    delta=0.50  v_DC - v_CD over 6 q's: ['-1/3', '-3/10', '-3/13', '-2/9', '-1/3', '-2/7']
    (at delta = 1 all of these are exactly 0 -- the equaliser; at delta < 1 they
     spread out, so no single constant is enforced.)

==============================================================================
(b')  WHERE DO DISCOUNTED FRIENDLY RIVALS EXIST?   brute force over (p0, p)
==============================================================================
  Efficient (discounted, eps -> 0): pi_delta(p,p) = Emax = max{1, (1+u+v)/2},
  with the round-0 state law of SELF-play x = (p0^2, p0(1-p0), (1-p0)p0, (1-p0)^2).
  Rival: min over (q, q0) of sign*(v_DC - v_CD) >= 0, sign = +1 if T > S else -1.

  delta = 9/10;  '.' = none, 'F' = a friendly rival exists
  wedge S = {u+v <= 1, u-v >= 1};  E = {u+v>1,u-v>1};  T>S <=> u-v<1

        u:  0.00 0.25 0.50 0.75 1.00 1.25 1.50 1.75 2.00 2.25 2.50 2.75 3.00
  v= 1.50:   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   =   .   . 
  v= 1.25:   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   =   .   .   . 
  v= 1.00:   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   =   .   .   .   . 
  v= 0.75:   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   =   .   .   .   .   . 
  v= 0.50:   .   .   .   .   .   .   =   .   .   .   .   .   . 
  v= 0.25:   .   .   .   .   .   =   .   .   .   .   .   .   . 
  v= 0.00:   .   .   .   .   =   .   .   .   .   .   .   .   . 
  v=-0.25:   .   .   .   =   F   F   .   .   .   .   .   .   . 
  v=-0.50:   .   .   =   F   F   F   F   .   .   .   .   .   . 
  v=-0.75:   .   =   F   F   F   F   F   F   .   .   .   .   . 
  v=-1.00:   =   F   F   F   F   F   F   F   F   .   .   .   . 
  v=-1.25:   F   F   F   F   F   F   F   F   F   F   .   .   . 
  v=-1.50:   F   F   F   F   F   F   F   F   F   F   F   .   . 

  Compare the UNDISCOUNTED result: friendly rivals exist exactly on the closed
  wedge S = {u-v >= 1, u+v <= 1} (plus the T=S line, where rivalry is vacuous).
  The '=' column is T = S (u - v = 1); on it every efficient strategy counts.

  Witness in wedge S: p = ALLC with p0 = 1.
    (u,v)=(3/2,0)  T-S=-1/2  efficient=False  rival=True
    (u,v)=(5/4,-1/2)  T-S=-3/4  efficient=True  rival=True
    (u,v)=(1,0)  T-S=0  efficient=True  rival=False

  Above the switch line (u+v > 1) discounted efficiency is EMPTY: Emax needs
  perfect alternation from round 0, but self-play round 0 has
  x_CC = p0^2 and x_DD = (1-p0)^2, which cannot both vanish.
    (u,v)=(3/2,1): Emax = 7/4, best self-play over 81 candidates = 335/294 = 1.1395

==============================================================================
(b'')  SIZE OF THE DISCOUNTED FRIENDLY-RIVAL SET INSIDE THE FACET p1 = 1
==============================================================================
  Friendly rival (wedge S interior, delta < 1, eps -> 0):
      p0 = 1,  p1 = 1,  p2 + p3 >= (2 delta - 1)/delta,  p4 FREE.
  Volume in the (p2,p3,p4) unit cube:  1                      delta <= 1/2
                                       1 - (2delta-1)^2/(2 delta^2)  delta > 1/2

    delta    threshold (2d-1)/d      volume    MC check
    0.250               -2.0000     1.00000     1.00000
    0.500                0.0000     1.00000     1.00000
    0.600                0.3333     0.94444     0.94647
    0.750                0.6667     0.77778     0.77900
    0.900                0.8889     0.60494     0.60755
    0.990                0.9899     0.51005     0.50935
    1.000                1.0000     0.50000     0.50557
  delta -> 1 gives 1/2, the project's undiscounted volume.  The set SHRINKS
  monotonically to the undiscounted one; it never disappears.

  Boundary case p = (1,1,0,0) with p0 = 1 -- EXCLUDED undiscounted by the
  'not (p2=1 and p3=0)' clause, but a rival for every delta < 1:
    delta= 0.500  min_q (v_CD - v_DC) =   0.00000000   rival=True
    delta= 0.900  min_q (v_CD - v_DC) =   0.00000000   rival=True
    delta= 0.990  min_q (v_CD - v_DC) =   0.00000000   rival=True
    delta= 0.999  min_q (v_CD - v_DC) =   0.00000000   rival=True
    delta=1, eps=0.01     min_q (W_CD - W_DC) =  -0.49000000   rival=False
    delta=1, eps=0.001    min_q (W_CD - W_DC) =  -0.49900000   rival=False
    delta=1, eps=0.0001   min_q (W_CD - W_DC) =  -0.49990000   rival=False
  with eps > 0 AND delta < 1 (p1 clamps to 1-eps < 1, so p1 = 1 fails):
    delta=0.9, eps=0.01     min_q (v_CD - v_DC) =  -0.06727119   rival=False
    delta=0.9, eps=0.001    min_q (v_CD - v_DC) =  -0.00794086   rival=False
  So the undiscounted exclusion of (p2,p3)=(1,0) is an ORDER-OF-LIMITS artefact:
    lim_{eps->0} at fixed delta < 1   -> rival (margin exactly 0)
    lim_{delta->1} at fixed eps > 0   -> not a rival (margin -> -1/2)
  The project's undiscounted theory is lim_{eps->0} lim_{delta->1}; the
  discounted theory here is lim_{eps->0} at delta < 1.  They do not commute on
  this measure-zero face, and only there.
